<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC "-//W3C//DTD XHTML 1.0 Transitional//EN" "http://www.w3.org/TR/xhtml1/DTD/xhtml1-transitional.dtd">
<html xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
<head>
  <meta http-equiv="Content-Type" content="text/html; charset=utf-8" />
  <title>Localist Social Calendar - Internal Error (500)</title>
  <style type="text/css">
    body, div, dl, dt, dd, ul, ol, li, h1, h2, h3, h4, h5, h6, pre, form, legend, fieldset, input, textarea, p, blockquote, th, td {
        margin: 0;
        padding: 0;
    }

    body.nopage {
      height: 100%;
      background-color: #fff;
      font-family: "Helvetica Neue", helvetica, arial, sans-serif;
    }

    .nocontent {
      background-color: #efefef;
      border: 1px solid #ddd;
      padding: 20px 0px 20px 0px;
      width: 80%;
      margin: 10px 0px 10px 10%;
      text-align: center;
      overflow: hidden;
    }

    .nopage .nocontent {
      border-width: 10px;
      background-color: #fafafa;
    }

    .nocontent h3 {
      color: #444;
      font-size: 16px;
      font-weight: bold;
    }

    .nocontent p {
      font-size: 14px;
      line-height: 20px;
      color: #444;
    }

    a {
        text-decoration: none;
        color: #3ea6e0;
    }

    .nopage h4 a {
      display: block;
      text-align: center;
      font: bold 20px/23px "Helvetica Neue", helvetica, arial, sans-serif;
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body class="nopage">
  <div class="nocontent nopage">
    <h3>Ouch! Something you clicked caused an internal problem (503)</h3>
    <p>Don't worry! It's not you, it's me.</p>
    <p>The issue has been sent to the people who built me, who will be applying fixes shortly.</p>
    <p><small>Please include this information when contacting support: XID: 11368169484 -- 503 -- Backend fetch failed</small></p>
  </div>
  <h4><a href="javascript:history.back()">Click here to go back to the last page you were on.</a></h4>
</body>
</html>